# Cursor rules for Portfolio v3

> Canonical cross-agent instructions: [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md)  
> UI design system: [`docs/ui/README.md`](./docs/ui/README.md)

You are an expert full-stack TypeScript engineer working on this Next.js project. Produce production-ready code that follows modern Next.js App Router patterns and best practices.

## Core directives

1. **Always refer to** [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md) and `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (Next.js, project management, unit testing, UI layout consistency).
2. Platform instruction map:
   - **All agents**: `AGENTS.md`
   - **Cursor**: `.cursorrules` + `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
   - **Claude**: `CLAUDE.md` + `.claude/`
   - **Gemini**: `.geminirules` / `GEMINI.md`
   - **Copilot**: `.github/copilot-instructions.md`
   - **UI docs**: `docs/ui/`
3. Adhere strictly to the Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript (strict mode), Tailwind CSS 3 (not v4) and shadcn/ui primitives restyled as monochrome Notion components.
4. Use **bun** as the package manager (`bun install`, `bun run test`, `bunx tsc --noEmit`). Never npm.

## Quick reference

- **React Server Components (RSC):** Default to Server Components. Add `'use client'` only when hook/state/browser interactivity is necessary.
- **Components:** Avoid inline styling. Rely wholly on Tailwind UI utilities and `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- **Architecture:** `app/` is for routes and layouts. `components/ui/` is for reusable shadcn widgets. Feature logic in `components/[feature]/` or `app/_components/`. Extract reusable hook logic to `lib/` or `hooks/`.
- **Quality:** Keep functions modular, readable, and typed. Do not rely on `any`.
- **Progress:** Read/update `prd/feature.md` and `prd/progress.md` for tracked work.

## UI rules (mandatory)

Read the UI rules in [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md#ui-rules-mandatory) and [`docs/ui/`](./docs/ui/README.md) before any UI work; they win over this file. The design is a **Notion workspace**: a grey sidebar, a thin top bar and Notion's 708px page column, monochrome in light and dark, set in one sans (Onest), with a photo as the home page's cover. The jest test `src/__tests__/unit/lib/ui-gate.test.ts` enforces it in CI through `bun run test`. The essentials:

- Every visitor page uses `BaseLayout`, a Notion workspace: a grey sidebar (`bg-muted`, 15rem, `lg` and up) with the owner's row, the pages with 16px lucide icons (`SECTION_ICONS`), a "More" group, contact rows, and at the bottom the legal links beside three theme icon radios (Sun, Moon, Monitor). From `lg` the « button (`CollapseToggle`) folds the sidebar to an icon rail; the state sits on `<html data-sidebar="collapsed">`, set before paint from localStorage `sidebar`. Below `lg`, a "Menu" button in the top bar opens the same tree in a left sheet. A 44px top bar with the breadcrumb and the theme toggle. The 708px page column (`width="wide"` on `/tools` and `/chat`), ending on one quiet line (year, Malang time, email).
- Every page opens with `PageHeader` (icon, 40px bold title via `text-title sm:text-display`, muted description). Content as Notion views and blocks: `Properties`, `LedgerList` / `LedgerRow` (list view), `MediaCard` in `Gallery` (gallery view), `Table` (table view), `ArticleShell` (article), `Callout` at most once per page. Each route's `loading.tsx` mirrors its page through `PageLoading` (the real icon and title, skeletons in the page's shapes).
- Monochrome: page text and links in ink (`text-foreground`, links through `InkLink`), secondary text in `text-muted-foreground`, hover `bg-tint`, tags and selected items `bg-tint-strong`, ink primary buttons. Colours only from the token classes; no hex, palette colours or `dark:` classes. Blue only in the text selection (`sky-wash`).
- Sizes only from the `fontSize` keys (small 14/20 for UI, body 16/24, prose 16/26, h2 24/32 at 600, page titles 40/48 at 700); weights 400 to 700; no `uppercase`, `tracking-[…]` or `text-[Npx]`. One sans, Onest; no serif, no handwritten face.
- Notion radii: 4px tags (`rounded`), 6px controls and rows (`rounded-md`), 10px cards, images and floating layers (`rounded-lg`); no `rounded-[…]`. Fields are 36px with a 3:1 `border-input`. No boxes around sections.
- No shadows anywhere: floating layers (dialog, sheet, menu, select) get a hairline border; the tooltip and toast are inverted. No blur and no gradients anywhere.
- The home cover is a photo (`PageCover`, `src/components/ui/page-cover.tsx`: 30vh, `next/image` with a blur placeholder), on the home page only. Motion is Notion's: fast row hovers (`duration-75`), menus and selects fade with a small zoom (0.97), dialogs fade and zoom, sheets slide fully, the sidebar width eases over 280ms, and content fades in over 300ms when it replaces a skeleton (`FADE_IN`). Reduced motion stops all of it. No motion libraries (framer-motion, `motion`, GSAP, Lenis).
- Auth (`/auth`, `/admin/auth/login`) follows notion.so/login: one 320px centred column, a two-line title, a full-width ink button, "or continue with" Google, then "New here? Create an account". The admin uses the same Notion shell: a grey sidebar with groups, a 44px top bar (breadcrumb, notifications bell, theme toggle), full-width content, and Notion tables with inline editors for collections.
- Copy in sentence case with plain verbs; no em dash in UI strings, no generic CTAs, no buzzwords.
- Umami: `data-umami-event` only on `<button>` and external `target="_blank"` links; internal links use `data-track`.

Platform shells (visitor, user, admin, auth): [`docs/ui/platforms.md`](./docs/ui/platforms.md)
